# Cloudflare Pages routing rules.
#
# US-191: /c/<id> share links are keyed by commitment UUID and are created by
# users long after the site is built, so they cannot be enumerated by
# getStaticPaths at build time. Rewrite every /c/<id> path to the static shell
# at /c/, which reads the id from the URL at runtime.
#
# Status 200 is a rewrite, not a redirect: the visitor's URL stays /c/<id>, so
# the page can still read the id and the shared link remains shareable.
/c/*  /c/index.html  200
